course: dictionary
lesson: 3481
title: Fame and being well known
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fame means being known about and talked about by very many people. Look at the words around it to work out what it means. «Vincent van Gogh sold very few paintings, and his fame grew after his death.» He sold few paintings while alive, so many people only came to know him after he died.
explain: Fame is a noun, a thing a person can have or win. You will often see it in phrases like «rise to fame» and «claim to fame». In «The world has held great Heroes», the song compares Toad's name with heroes, so fame means being famous, known by many.
explain: Fame is not always fair or quick. «Fame is not fair or quick» tells you that a person can become well known slowly, and not always for good reasons. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: if «being well known» still makes sense, you have got it.
fact: Fame means being known about and talked about by very many people.
fact: «Rise to fame» means becoming well known.
fact: «Hall of fame» is a place that honours people who are famous for great deeds.
fact: Being famous does not always mean being happy: «Van Gogh's fame grew after his death.»
fact: Fame is a noun, and it is uncountable, so we do not say «a fame» or «fames».
exercise: Ella says fame means having lots of money. What does fame really mean? | Being very quiet and shy | *Being known about and talked about by very many people | Having lots of money in the bank | Being very tall and strong
exercise: Which phrase means that someone has become well known? | sleep for a whole week | *rise to fame | run away very quickly | make a cake for a friend
exercise: «Vincent van Gogh sold very few paintings, and his fame grew after his death.» What does this tell you? | He never painted anything at all | *Many people came to know him only after he died | He was famous for one single day | He was famous as a small child
test: How old was Vincent van Gogh when he died? | 71 | 53 | 1890 | *37
test: «Christians believe nothing should take God's place, not money, fame or things.» In this list, what is fame? | A type of tune | *Being well known by many people | A kind of food | Being very quiet
exam: In «Very high art prices come from fame, history, rarity and buyers competing at auctions», what is fame one reason for? | *Very high art prices | Art being painted very fast | Fewer paintings being sold | People forgetting the artists
